IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `epbc-claims-dates`
IMPORT `epbc-claims`

-- Environment Protection and Biodiversity Conservation Act 1999 (Cth) -- worked cases for the questions of the person
-- bringing a claim (ss 475-479, 487, 488, 499(3), 500).
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the dates used below`

`1 Jan 2020` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 1 2020
`9 Mar 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 9 3 2024
`10 Mar 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 10 3 2024
`31 May 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 31 5 2024
`1 Jun 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 6 2024
`15 Jun 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 15 6 2024
`30 Jun 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 30 6 2024
`1 Jul 2024` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 7 2024
`27 Feb 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 27 2 2026
`28 Feb 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 28 2 2026
`9 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 9 3 2026
`10 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 10 3 2026
`11 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 11 3 2026
`1 May 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 5 2026
`31 May 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 31 5 2026
`1 Jun 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 6 2026
`30 Jun 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 30 6 2026
`1 Jul 2026` MEANS `the calendar day` 1 7 2026
`29 Feb 2028` MEANS `the calendar day` 29 2 2028

§ `Short names for the answers`

`IP YES A` MEANS `yes: you are an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident, and your interests have been, are or would be affected by the conduct (s 475(6)(a))`
`IP YES B` MEANS `yes: you are an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident, and you engaged in a series of activities for the environment in the 2 years immediately before the conduct or, for proposed conduct, the application (s 475(6)(b))`
`IP NO CITIZEN` MEANS `no: you are neither an Australian citizen nor ordinarily resident in Australia or an external Territory (s 475(6), the text's no)`
`IP NO ACTIVITIES` MEANS `no: your interests are not affected and you have not engaged in a series of activities for the environment (s 475(6), the text's no)`
`IP NO WINDOW` MEANS `no: your interests are not affected and your last activity for the environment was outside the 2 years immediately before the conduct or, for proposed conduct, the application (s 475(6)(b), the text's no)`

`INJ YES` MEANS `yes: as an interested person you may apply to the Federal Court for an injunction (s 475(1)(b))`
`INJ NO CONTRAVENTION` MEANS `no: the conduct is not an offence or other contravention of the Act or the regulations, so s 475 gives no injunction (s 475(1), the text's no)`
`INJ NOT SHOWN` MEANS `not shown: you are not an interested person, and s 475(1) gives standing only to the persons it names; other remedies are outside this encoding (s 475(1), NOTHING-kind)`

`ORG YES INC` MEANS `yes: the organisation is an interested person and, being incorporated, may itself apply to the Federal Court for an injunction (s 475(1)(b), (7))`
`ORG YES UNINC` MEANS `yes: the organisation is an interested person and, being unincorporated, a person acting on its behalf (such as you) may apply to the Federal Court for an injunction (s 475(1)(c), (7))`
`ORG NO CONTRAVENTION` MEANS `no: the conduct is not an offence or other contravention of the Act or the regulations, so s 475 gives the organisation no injunction (s 475(1), the text's no)`
`ORG NO ESTABLISHED` MEANS `no: the organisation is not incorporated or otherwise established in Australia or an external Territory, so it is not an interested person (s 475(7), the text's no)`
`ORG NO CONDITION` MEANS `no: the organisation's interests are not affected, and it did not have environmental objects and carry on a series of environmental activities in the 2 years immediately before the conduct or, for proposed conduct, the application (s 475(7), the text's no)`

`ORDERS PROHIBITORY` MEANS `the court may grant an injunction restraining the person from the conduct, and if it thinks it desirable order the person to do something, including repair or mitigate damage to the environment; it may grant an interim injunction before deciding; it need not find that the person intends to continue or did it before, or that there is a significant risk of injury or damage (ss 475(2), (3), (5), 479(1)); the injunction may later be discharged or varied on application (s 477); a remediation order under s 480A is for the CEO or the Director to seek`
`ORDERS MANDATORY` MEANS `the court may grant an injunction requiring the person to do the act; it may grant an interim injunction before deciding; it need not find that the person intends to refuse or fail again or did so before, or that there is a significant risk of injury or damage (ss 475(4), (5), 479(2)); the injunction may later be discharged or varied on application (s 477); a remediation order under s 480A is for the CEO or the Director to seek`
`ORDERS NONE` MEANS `none under s 475: the conduct, refusal or failure is not an offence or other contravention of the Act or the regulations (s 475(2), (4), the text's no)`

`CA YES` MEANS `yes: as another person bound by the agreement you may apply to the Federal Court for an injunction; the court may restrain the conduct (with an order to repair or mitigate damage if desirable), order the party to do the act, or grant an interim injunction (s 476(1)(a), (2)-(5))`
`CA NO CONTRAVENTION` MEANS `no: the conduct is not a contravention of the conservation agreement (s 476(1), the text's no)`
`CA NO OTHER NOT BOUND` MEANS `no: the person acting is not bound by the conservation agreement (s 476(1), the text's no)`
`CA NOT SHOWN ME` MEANS `not shown: you are not bound by the agreement, and s 476(1) gives standing only to another person bound, the CEO and the Director (NOTHING-kind)`
`CA NOT SHOWN PAST` MEANS `not shown: s 476(1) speaks of a party who engages or proposes to engage in the conduct; conduct that is wholly past is not within its words, though s 476(2) speaks of a party who has engaged (fork F4, NOTHING-kind)`

`PA YES` MEANS `yes: you are taken to be a person aggrieved by the decision, failure or conduct, and may apply for review under the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977 (s 487(2))`
`PA NOT CITIZEN` MEANS `not shown by s 487: you are not an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident; you may still be a person aggrieved under the ADJR Act's own meaning, which s 487 extends and does not limit (s 487(1), NOTHING-kind)`
`PA NO ACTIVITIES` MEANS `not shown by s 487: you have not engaged in a series of environmental activities in Australia or an external Territory; you may still be a person aggrieved under the ADJR Act's own meaning (s 487(1), NOTHING-kind)`
`PA NO WINDOW` MEANS `not shown by s 487: your last environmental activity was outside the 2 years immediately before the decision, failure or conduct; you may still be a person aggrieved under the ADJR Act's own meaning (s 487(1), NOTHING-kind)`

`REV YES INC` MEANS `yes: the organisation is taken to be a person aggrieved and, being incorporated, may itself apply for review under the ADJR Act (s 487(3))`
`REV YES UNINC` MEANS `yes: the organisation is taken to be a person aggrieved and, being unincorporated, a person acting on its behalf (such as you) may apply for review, as if a person aggrieved (ss 487(3), 488)`
`REV NOT SHOWN` MEANS `not shown by s 487: the organisation does not meet s 487(3); it may still be a person aggrieved under the ADJR Act's own meaning, and if it is and is unincorporated, a person acting on its behalf may apply (ss 487(1), 488, NOTHING-kind)`

`LOSS YES` MEANS `yes: the person who contravened the Act is liable to pay you an amount equal to your loss or damage; it is a debt due to you, recoverable in a court of competent jurisdiction (s 500(1), (3))`
`LOSS YES 499` MEANS `yes: the damage or condition is taken to arise from the false or misleading information given in contravention of s 489, so the person who gave it is liable to pay you an amount equal to your loss or damage arising from it, as a debt recoverable in a court of competent jurisdiction (ss 499(3), 500(1), (3))`
`LOSS NO DECISION` MEANS `no: s 500 does not apply to a decision, a failure to make a decision, or conduct for the purposes of making a decision, purportedly under the Act (s 500(7), the text's no)`
`LOSS NOT SHOWN CONTRAVENTION` MEANS `not shown: no contravention of the Act or the regulations is established, and s 500 is silent about such a case (s 500(1), NOTHING-kind)`
`LOSS NOT SHOWN ARISING` MEANS `not shown: your loss or damage is not shown to arise from the contravention, and s 500 is silent about such a case (s 500(1), NOTHING-kind)`

`WHOM ONE` MEANS `the one person liable must pay you the whole amount (s 500(1))`
`WHOM JOINT` MEANS `the persons liable are jointly and severally liable: you may recover the whole sum from any one of them, or from them together, but not more than the sum in all (s 500(4))`
`WHOM NONE` MEANS `not shown: no person is liable to you under s 500(1) on these facts (NOTHING-kind)`

`FINDING YES` MEANS `yes: the court's finding in the criminal or civil proceedings that the wrongdoer contravened the Act or the regulations is admissible as evidence of the contravention in your proceedings to recover (admissible, not conclusive) (s 500(5))`
`FINDING NOT SHOWN` MEANS `not shown: there is no earlier court finding that the wrongdoer contravened the Act or the regulations; s 500(5) does not help, and the contravention must be proved (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `The 2 years immediately before (fork F1: the first day counts, the end day does not; fork F2: 29 February)`

#ASSERT `the first day of the 2 years before` `10 Mar 2026` EQUALS `10 Mar 2024`
#ASSERT `the first day of the 2 years before` `29 Feb 2028` EQUALS `28 Feb 2026`
#ASSERT `10 Mar 2024` `falls in the 2 years immediately before` `10 Mar 2026`
#ASSERT (NOT (`9 Mar 2024` `falls in the 2 years immediately before` `10 Mar 2026`))
#ASSERT `9 Mar 2026` `falls in the 2 years immediately before` `10 Mar 2026`
#ASSERT (NOT (`10 Mar 2026` `falls in the 2 years immediately before` `10 Mar 2026`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`11 Mar 2026` `falls in the 2 years immediately before` `10 Mar 2026`))
#ASSERT `28 Feb 2026` `falls in the 2 years immediately before` `29 Feb 2028`
#ASSERT (NOT (`27 Feb 2026` `falls in the 2 years immediately before` `29 Feb 2028`))

§ `s 475(6) -- am I an interested person`

-- A resident whose water supply is affected by the conduct: (a), with no activities at all.
#ASSERT `s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `10 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `IP YES A`
-- A visitor neither a citizen nor ordinarily resident, though affected.
#ASSERT `s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` FALSE TRUE TRUE `10 Mar 2026` FALSE `10 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `IP NO CITIZEN`
-- A citizen not affected, with no environmental activities.
#ASSERT `s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `10 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `IP NO ACTIVITIES`
-- A volunteer whose last activity was exactly 2 years before the conduct (10 Mar 2024 for conduct on 10 Mar 2026): in.
#ASSERT `s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` TRUE FALSE TRUE `10 Mar 2024` FALSE `10 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `IP YES B`
-- One day earlier (9 Mar 2024): out.
#ASSERT `s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` TRUE FALSE TRUE `9 Mar 2024` FALSE `10 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `IP NO WINDOW`
-- Proposed conduct: the 2 years run back from the application (1 Jun 2026), so from 1 Jun 2024.
#ASSERT `s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` TRUE FALSE TRUE `15 Jun 2024` TRUE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `IP YES B`
#ASSERT `s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` TRUE FALSE TRUE `1 Jun 2024` TRUE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `IP YES B`
#ASSERT `s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` TRUE FALSE TRUE `31 May 2024` TRUE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `IP NO WINDOW`
-- The same last activity (31 May 2024) against conduct that happened on 1 May 2026: from 1 May 2024, so in.
#ASSERT `s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` TRUE FALSE TRUE `31 May 2024` FALSE `1 May 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `IP YES B`
-- A volunteer active every week since 2020 and still active; conduct on 10 Mar 2026. The input asks for the latest
-- activity day before the conduct, 9 Mar 2026: in. Continuing activity after the conduct does not turn the person away.
#ASSERT `s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` TRUE FALSE TRUE `9 Mar 2026` FALSE `10 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `IP YES B`
-- The same volunteer, proposed conduct, application on 1 Jun 2026: latest activity day before it, 31 May 2026: in.
#ASSERT `s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` TRUE FALSE TRUE `31 May 2026` TRUE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `IP YES B`
-- A day given that is not before the conduct (the conduct day itself) is outside the window (fork F1).
#ASSERT `s 475(6) -- am I an interested person` TRUE FALSE TRUE `10 Mar 2026` FALSE `10 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `IP NO WINDOW`

§ `s 475(1) -- can I apply for an injunction`

#ASSERT `s 475(1) -- can I apply for an injunction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `10 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `INJ YES`
#ASSERT `s 475(1) -- can I apply for an injunction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `10 Mar 2024` FALSE `10 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `INJ YES`
#ASSERT `s 475(1) -- can I apply for an injunction` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `10 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `INJ NO CONTRAVENTION`
#ASSERT `s 475(1) -- can I apply for an injunction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `9 Mar 2024` FALSE `10 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `INJ NOT SHOWN`
#ASSERT `s 475(1) -- can I apply for an injunction` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `10 Mar 2026` FALSE `10 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `INJ NOT SHOWN`
#ASSERT `s 475(1) -- can I apply for an injunction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `15 Jun 2024` TRUE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `INJ YES`

§ `s 475(7) -- can my organisation apply for an injunction`

-- An incorporated local landcare association whose site is affected.
#ASSERT `s 475(7) -- can my organisation apply for an injunction` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `ORG YES INC`
-- The same, unincorporated: I apply on its behalf.
#ASSERT `s 475(7) -- can my organisation apply for an injunction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `ORG YES UNINC`
-- Not affected; environmental objects and activities up to 1 Jul 2024, conduct on 1 Jul 2026: the first day counts.
#ASSERT `s 475(7) -- can my organisation apply for an injunction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `1 Jul 2024` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `ORG YES INC`
-- Still active after the conduct of 1 Jul 2026: latest activity day before it, 30 Jun 2026: in.
#ASSERT `s 475(7) -- can my organisation apply for an injunction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `30 Jun 2026` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `ORG YES INC`
-- Last activity 30 Jun 2024: out.
#ASSERT `s 475(7) -- can my organisation apply for an injunction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `30 Jun 2024` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `ORG NO CONDITION`
-- Proposed conduct, application on 1 Jun 2026: the window runs from 1 Jun 2024, so 30 Jun 2024 is in.
#ASSERT `s 475(7) -- can my organisation apply for an injunction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `30 Jun 2024` TRUE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `ORG YES UNINC`
-- No environmental objects and activities, not affected.
#ASSERT `s 475(7) -- can my organisation apply for an injunction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `ORG NO CONDITION`
-- An organisation established overseas, though affected.
#ASSERT `s 475(7) -- can my organisation apply for an injunction` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `ORG NO ESTABLISHED`
-- No contravention.
#ASSERT `s 475(7) -- can my organisation apply for an injunction` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `1 Jul 2026` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `ORG NO CONTRAVENTION`

§ `ss 475(2)-(5), 479 -- what can the court order`

#ASSERT `ss 475, 479 -- what can the court order` `engaged in an act` TRUE EQUALS `ORDERS PROHIBITORY`
#ASSERT `ss 475, 479 -- what can the court order` `is engaging in an act` TRUE EQUALS `ORDERS PROHIBITORY`
#ASSERT `ss 475, 479 -- what can the court order` `proposes to engage in an act` TRUE EQUALS `ORDERS PROHIBITORY`
#ASSERT `ss 475, 479 -- what can the court order` `refused or failed to do an act` TRUE EQUALS `ORDERS MANDATORY`
#ASSERT `ss 475, 479 -- what can the court order` `is refusing or failing to do an act` TRUE EQUALS `ORDERS MANDATORY`
#ASSERT `ss 475, 479 -- what can the court order` `proposes to refuse or fail to do an act` TRUE EQUALS `ORDERS MANDATORY`
#ASSERT `ss 475, 479 -- what can the court order` `is engaging in an act` FALSE EQUALS `ORDERS NONE`
#ASSERT `ss 475, 479 -- what can the court order` `refused or failed to do an act` FALSE EQUALS `ORDERS NONE`

§ `s 476 -- can I seek an injunction under the agreement`

-- A landholder who signed the agreement; a neighbouring co-signatory is clearing covered vegetation now.
#ASSERT `s 476 -- can I seek an injunction under the agreement` `I entered into the agreement with the Minister` TRUE `the other party is now acting or failing to act` TRUE EQUALS `CA YES`
-- A buyer of part of the covered land (s 307(c)); the other party proposes to clear.
#ASSERT `s 476 -- can I seek an injunction under the agreement` `I am a successor to an interest in a place the agreement covers` TRUE `the other party proposes to act or fail to act` TRUE EQUALS `CA YES`
-- Clearing that has stopped (fork F4).
#ASSERT `s 476 -- can I seek an injunction under the agreement` `I entered into the agreement with the Minister` TRUE `the other party acted or failed to act in the past but has stopped` TRUE EQUALS `CA NOT SHOWN PAST`
-- A neighbour not bound.
#ASSERT `s 476 -- can I seek an injunction under the agreement` `I am not bound by the agreement` TRUE `the other party is now acting or failing to act` TRUE EQUALS `CA NOT SHOWN ME`
-- The person acting is not bound.
#ASSERT `s 476 -- can I seek an injunction under the agreement` `I entered into the agreement with the Minister` FALSE `the other party is now acting or failing to act` TRUE EQUALS `CA NO OTHER NOT BOUND`
-- No contravention of the agreement.
#ASSERT `s 476 -- can I seek an injunction under the agreement` `I entered into the agreement with the Minister` TRUE `the other party is now acting or failing to act` FALSE EQUALS `CA NO CONTRAVENTION`

§ `s 487(2) -- am I a person aggrieved`

#ASSERT `s 487(2) -- am I a person aggrieved` TRUE TRUE `10 Mar 2024` `10 Mar 2026` EQUALS `PA YES`
#ASSERT `s 487(2) -- am I a person aggrieved` TRUE TRUE `9 Mar 2024` `10 Mar 2026` EQUALS `PA NO WINDOW`
-- Active weekly in Australia and still active after a decision of 1 Jul 2026: latest activity day before it, 30 Jun 2026: in.
#ASSERT `s 487(2) -- am I a person aggrieved` TRUE TRUE `30 Jun 2026` `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `PA YES`
-- The decision day itself is not before the decision (fork F1).
#ASSERT `s 487(2) -- am I a person aggrieved` TRUE TRUE `10 Mar 2026` `10 Mar 2026` EQUALS `PA NO WINDOW`
-- A decision on 29 Feb 2028: the 2 years run from 28 Feb 2026 (fork F2).
#ASSERT `s 487(2) -- am I a person aggrieved` TRUE TRUE `28 Feb 2026` `29 Feb 2028` EQUALS `PA YES`
#ASSERT `s 487(2) -- am I a person aggrieved` TRUE TRUE `27 Feb 2026` `29 Feb 2028` EQUALS `PA NO WINDOW`
#ASSERT `s 487(2) -- am I a person aggrieved` FALSE TRUE `10 Mar 2026` `10 Mar 2026` EQUALS `PA NOT CITIZEN`
-- Activities only overseas: not within s 487(2)(b) (contrast s 475(6)(b), finding 2).
#ASSERT `s 487(2) -- am I a person aggrieved` TRUE FALSE `10 Mar 2026` `10 Mar 2026` EQUALS `PA NO ACTIVITIES`

§ `ss 487(3), 488 -- can my organisation seek review`

#ASSERT `ss 487(3), 488 -- can my organisation seek review` TRUE TRUE TRUE `1 Jul 2024` TRUE `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `REV YES INC`
#ASSERT `ss 487(3), 488 -- can my organisation seek review` TRUE FALSE TRUE `1 Jul 2024` TRUE `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `REV YES UNINC`
#ASSERT `ss 487(3), 488 -- can my organisation seek review` TRUE TRUE TRUE `30 Jun 2024` TRUE `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `REV NOT SHOWN`
-- An organisation still active after the decision of 1 Jul 2026: latest activity day before it, 30 Jun 2026: in.
#ASSERT `ss 487(3), 488 -- can my organisation seek review` TRUE TRUE TRUE `30 Jun 2026` TRUE `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `REV YES INC`
-- Environmental objects adopted only after the decision: (c) fails.
#ASSERT `ss 487(3), 488 -- can my organisation seek review` TRUE TRUE TRUE `1 Jun 2026` FALSE `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `REV NOT SHOWN`
#ASSERT `ss 487(3), 488 -- can my organisation seek review` FALSE FALSE TRUE `1 Jun 2026` TRUE `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `REV NOT SHOWN`
#ASSERT `ss 487(3), 488 -- can my organisation seek review` TRUE FALSE FALSE `1 Jun 2026` TRUE `1 Jul 2026` EQUALS `REV NOT SHOWN`

§ `s 500 -- can I recover my loss`

-- A fishing business whose catch fell after unlawful discharge into a wetland: contravention and loss arising.
#ASSERT `s 500 -- can I recover my loss` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `LOSS YES`
-- The grant of the approval itself (s 500(7)), even if said to contravene the Act.
#ASSERT `s 500 -- can I recover my loss` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `LOSS NO DECISION`
-- Approval obtained with false information (s 489); granted unaware; the action damaged the wetland; my loss arose from it.
#ASSERT `s 500 -- can I recover my loss` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `LOSS YES 499`
-- The same, but the Minister was not shown to be unaware: no deeming, and no other link shown.
#ASSERT `s 500 -- can I recover my loss` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `LOSS NOT SHOWN ARISING`
-- A contravention, but my loss did not arise from it.
#ASSERT `s 500 -- can I recover my loss` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `LOSS NOT SHOWN ARISING`
-- No contravention at all.
#ASSERT `s 500 -- can I recover my loss` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `LOSS NOT SHOWN CONTRAVENTION`

§ `s 500(1), (2) -- how much am I owed`

-- $10,000 lost income, $2,500 to remove a spill, $1,500 to fence off a creek, nothing on prevention: $14,000.
#ASSERT `s 500(1), (2) -- how much am I owed` 10000 2500 1500 0 EQUALS 14000
#ASSERT `s 500(1), (2) -- how much am I owed` 0 0 0 3200 EQUALS 3200
#ASSERT `s 500(1), (2) -- how much am I owed` 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 0

§ `s 500(4) -- whom can I recover from`

#ASSERT `s 500(4) -- whom can I recover from` 0 EQUALS `WHOM NONE`
#ASSERT `s 500(4) -- whom can I recover from` 1 EQUALS `WHOM ONE`
#ASSERT `s 500(4) -- whom can I recover from` 2 EQUALS `WHOM JOINT`
#ASSERT `s 500(4) -- whom can I recover from` 5 EQUALS `WHOM JOINT`

§ `s 500(5) -- can I use the earlier finding`

#ASSERT `s 500(5) -- can I use the earlier finding` TRUE EQUALS `FINDING YES`
#ASSERT `s 500(5) -- can I use the earlier finding` FALSE EQUALS `FINDING NOT SHOWN`
